UPDATE sections SET data = '{"eyebrow":"Local Knowledge","title":"Remodeling in Ridgefield, Connecticut","content":"Ridgefield''s residential areas feature colonials, contemporaries, and wooded estate homes built from the 1950s through the 2000s. Many homes sit on large, wooded lots with private settings. The housing stock reflects a mix of mid-century builds needing comprehensive updates and newer homes ready for kitchen and bathroom refreshes. Larger properties often include finished basements, home offices, and in-law suites.\\\\n\\\\nRidgefield is a picturesque New England town in northern Fairfield County, known for its charming Main Street, Aldrich Contemporary Art Museum, and well-regarded schools. Homeowners here tend to stay long-term and invest in their properties over time. The Ridgefield Building Department has specific requirements for properties near wetlands and in the historic district, and we address those requirements during the initial planning phase.\\\\n\\\\nRidgefield is about 40 minutes from our Orange office. That proximity means faster response times, no travel delays, and direct familiarity with Ridgefield''s housing stock and building department requirements. When you call us about a project in Ridgefield, you''re reaching a team that already knows the conditions your home is likely to present.","image":null,"image_alt":null,"image_position":"right","cta":null,"align":"center","variant":"default","style_variant":"default","surface":"default","container_width":"narrow","spacing":"normal","anchor_id":null}', updated_at = NOW() WHERE id = 3701;
